  "title": "Rain Rot Disease Cases Rise in Europe: Experts Warn of Emerging Sexually Transmitted Skin Infection",
  "summary": "Rain Rot Disease Cases Increase Across Europe, Raising Public Health Concerns Health experts are warning about a rare bacterial skin infection, commonly known as rain rot disease, after a growing number of human cases were identified in several European countries. The infection, medically known as dermatophilosis, has traditionally affected livestock and wildlife, but researchers say recent clusters suggest it may now be spreading through close skin-to-skin contact, including sexual activity.",
